{% doc %}
  Prints `true` when the visitor's country is one of the countries listed in
  Theme settings > Cart > Countries with free shipping, and nothing otherwise.
  Capture it, since a snippet can't return a value, and test the capture with
  `contains`: it can carry a stray newline from this file.

  The free shipping rates only exist for Europe. A visitor from the US or
  Canada pays a flat rate at checkout, so every "free shipping over €100"
  message checks this first instead of promising it to everyone.

  @example
  {% capture free_ship_here %}{% render 'free-shipping-eligible' %}{% endcapture %}
  {% if free_ship_here contains 'true' %}…{% endif %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign free_ship_countries = settings.free_shipping_countries | strip_newlines | remove: ' ' | upcase | split: ','
  if free_ship_countries contains localization.country.iso_code
    echo 'true'
  endif
-%}
